1. What is the purpose of using document.getElementById() in the calculator?
It helps JavaScript find something in the calculator. It can find the input boxes and buttons. This lets JavaScript use them.

2. Why do we use Number() before performing the calculation?
Number() changes the input into a number. This helps JavaScript do the math correctly. Without it, the input may be treated as text.

3. How do HTML, CSS, and JavaScript work together in this activity?
HTML makes the calculator parts. CSS makes the calculator look nice. JavaScript makes the calculator work.